.TH MKTORRENT 1 "November 2026" "MKTorrent @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mktorrent \- create BitTorrent metainfo files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mktorrent
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR|\fIDIRECTORY\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mktorrent
is a simple command-line utility to create BitTorrent metainfo files.
It supports both single file and directory torrents, with configurable piece
length and multiple announce URLs. Announce URLs are optional (DHT-only torrents).
Linux only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-announce\fR=\fIURL\fR
Add an announce URL. Can be used multiple times. Optional; omit for DHT-only torrents.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-comment\fR=\fICOMMENT\fR
Add a comment to the metainfo (max 65536 bytes; no control characters).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-no\-date\fR
Don't write the creation date.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-no\-created\-by\fR
Don't write the created-by field.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-exclude\fR=\fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude files whose basename or relative path matches the shell pattern
(see \fBglob\fR(7)). Can be used multiple times. Wins over \fB\-\-include\fR.
At most 256 patterns, each ≤ 1024 bytes. Example: \fBsubdir/*.tmp\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-include\fR=\fIPATTERN\fR
Only include regular files whose basename or relative path matches the shell
pattern. Directories are still walked so nested matches work. Same pattern
caps as \fB\-\-exclude\fR. Can be used multiple times.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-hidden\fR
Skip any basename starting with \fB.\fR (files and directories). Default is to
include hidden names other than \fB.\fR and \fB..\fR.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite the output file if it already exists (truncated).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-piece\-length\fR=\fIN\fR
Piece length as an exponent 15–28 (\fB2^N\fR bytes), or as a byte size with
optional \fBK\fR/\fBM\fR/\fBG\fR suffix (1024-based). Byte forms must be a power
of two in [32 KiB, 256 MiB]. Examples: \fB\-l 20\fR, \fB\-l 1M\fR, \fB\-l 1048576\fR.
Default is chosen automatically from the total size.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR=\fINAME\fR
Set the name of the torrent. Default is basename of FILE or DIRECTORY.
Required when multiple targets, \fB\-\-from\-file\fR, or \fB\-\-stdin\fR are used.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Set the path of the created .torrent file.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-private\fR
Set the private flag.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress progress and success messages (errors still go to stderr).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-source\fR=\fISOURCE\fR
Set the source string.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR=\fINUM\fR
Set the number of threads to use for hashing (default: number of CPU cores, max 64).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
After a successful create, print a single JSON object on stdout
(fields: ok, path, name, length, pieceLength, pieces, private, infoHash,
announce, nodes). Suppresses other stdout noise.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-web\-seed\fR=\fIURL\fR
Add a web seed URL. Can be used multiple times.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-cross\-seed\fR
Ensure the info hash is unique for easier cross-seeding.
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Read target paths from FILE (one path per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored).
Requires \fB\-n\fR / \fB\-\-name\fR. With \fB\-0\fR / \fB\-\-null\fR, paths are NUL-separated and # comments are not special.
Overlong lines without a newline are rejected.
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
Read target paths from standard input (same rules as \fB\-\-from\-file\fR).
Requires \fB\-n\fR / \fB\-\-name\fR. May be combined with positional targets.
.TP
\fB\-0\fR, \fB\-\-null\fR
NUL-separate paths for \fB\-\-from\-file\fR and \fB\-\-stdin\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-follow\-symlinks\fR
Do not follow symbolic links; skip them with a warning.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-files\fR=\fIN\fR
Refuse after N files are queued (default 1000000).
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR=\fIN\fR
Refuse if aggregate size exceeds N bytes (0 = unlimited).
.TP
\fB\-\-node\fR=\fIHOST:PORT\fR
Add a DHT bootstrap node (BEP 5 \fBnodes\fR list). Repeatable.
.TP
\fB\-\-direct\-io\fR
Use O_DIRECT for large files when supported (opt-in; default is buffered I/O).
.TP
\fB\-\-io\-uring\fR
Use io_uring for piece reads (Linux build with liburing; never the default).
.TP
\fB\-\-io\-uring\-depth\fR=\fIN\fR
io_uring queue depth (1–256, default 32). Requires \fB\-\-io\-uring\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-io\-uring\-sqpoll\fR
Experimental \fBIORING_SETUP_SQPOLL\fR. Requires \fB\-\-io\-uring\fR; setup failure is fatal.
.TP
\fB\-\-sha1\fR=\fIauto\fR|\fIopenssl\fR|\fIisal\fR
Select the piece SHA-1 implementation (pthread builds). Default \fBauto\fR uses OpenSSL when
linked, otherwise the bundled SHA-1. \fBisal\fR requires a build with ISA-L Crypto and selects
batched multi-buffer piece hashing (hash workers capped at 1–2). \fBopenssl\fR selects OpenSSL
or the bundled implementation when OpenSSL was not linked. \fB\-V\fR prints the active backend.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage or argument error.
.TP
.B 2
I/O, hashing, or write failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a torrent for a single file:
.B mktorrent \-a http://tracker.example.com/announce \-o file.torrent file.iso
.TP
Create a torrent for a directory:
.B mktorrent \-a http://tracker.example.com/announce \-o dir.torrent directory/
.TP
Create a private torrent with 1 MiB pieces:
.B mktorrent \-a http://tracker.example.com/announce \-p \-l 1M \-o private.torrent file.iso
.TP
Create a DHT-only torrent with a bootstrap node and emit JSON:
.B mktorrent \-\-json \-\-node 127.0.0.1:6881 \-o out.torrent file.iso
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bittorrent (7),
.BR transmission\-cli (1)
